Selected scenario
Construct ConversationEngine with FailingClient and ThrowingDiagnosticSink.
Register StatusObserver.OnStatusChanged, then await SendMessageAsync.
These are the only implementations in scope for this bounded scenario.

Originating issue
Report conversation-processing failures through the configured diagnostic sink.

Target-base contract
Processing failures are exposed in Error and the Error status; notify status observers.

PR rationale and test
The author says the nested catch preserves successful task completion.
A new test awaits SendMessageAsync and asserts that Error is the client's Failure.
Its complete implementation follows below.

Existing feedback
None.

using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Xunit;

public class ConversationEngineTests
{
    [Fact]
    public async Task ProcessingFailureIsExposed()
    {
        var client = new FailingClient();
        var sink = new ThrowingDiagnosticSink();
        var observer = new StatusObserver();
        var engine = new ConversationEngine(client, sink);
        engine.StatusChanged += observer.OnStatusChanged;

        await engine.SendMessageAsync();

        Assert.Same(client.Failure, engine.Error);
        Assert.Equal("Error", engine.Status);
        Assert.Equal(1, observer.NotificationCount);
    }
}
